From 542b2fba384dc7251832e2d924d19b53e0737eb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: masumi <masumi@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:48:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] dspark: record the drafter's pre-Markov base logit top-k in
 the draft trace

The trace already keeps the target's top-k logits (the U_k the Markov head is
fitted as a residual on). The drafter side of that residual was missing: the
Markov bias is added to the drafter's own base logits, and those never left
the GPU.

Capture them in DSparkSpeculator._sample_sequential, right after the base
logits are viewed as (num_reqs, n_spec, vocab) and before the Markov loop
touches them: rows are (req, step) flattened, values float32, ids int32, k
default 32. The vocabulary-parallel greedy path only reduces (max, index)
shard pairs and never materialises full-vocabulary logits, so a captured step
turns that path off and takes the dense compute_draft_logits route; the flag
is False whenever the trace or the drafter dump is off, which is the default,
and then the drafting path is bit-for-bit the one that ran before.

DSparkTrace.record writes the block to <path>.drafttopk.f32/.i32, next to the
target dump but in files of its own, and puts one dl block {off, rows, k, n}
on the lines of that step. Width comes from SPARK3_DSPARK_TRACE_DRAFTTOPK or
the /cache/dspark-trace/DRAFTTOPK marker (0 disables it), independent of the
target dump's TOPK. A step that captured nothing records dx: 1 instead of
inheriting the previous step's block.
---
 vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py            |  23 +++
 .../gpu/spec_decode/dspark/speculator.py      |  39 +++++
 .../v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dspark/trace.py | 143 +++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 198 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

